# --- s038 Book I d.9 q.un. = Ord. I d.9 q.un.
n("n636","s038-01","Circa nonam distinctionem","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 9 q. un., *utrum generatio Filii sit aeterna* (Vat. IV).","to-verify")
n("n637","s038-01","ante luciferum genui te","la","source","Ps. 109:3 (Vulg.): *ex utero ante luciferum genui te*.","certain")
n("n638","s038-01","ab initio et ante secula creata sum","la","source","Ecclus. (Sir.) 24:14 (Vulg.): *ab initio et ante saecula creata sum*, quoted as *liber sapientie* in the broad sense of the sapiential books. Prov. 8:22–25 (*Dominus possedit me in initio…*).","certain")
n("n639","s038-02","Gregorium","la","source","Gregory the Great, *Moralia in Iob* XXIX (on Job 38). Gorris corrects Scotus's attribution. The passage is not on Job 38:21 (*sciebas tunc quod nasciturus esses*) but on Job 38:12, a little earlier in the same chapter and the same book of the *Moralia*. The verse is *numquid post ortum tuum praecepisti diluculo et ostendisti aurorae locum suum*. This is a notable piece of source-criticism by Gorris; the exact locus in *Moralia* XXIX is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n640","s038-02","Sciebat","la","textual","A has *Sciebas* in the first quotation and *Sciebat* in the second (B has *Sciebas* in the first; the second not checked). The Vulgate (Job 38:21) reads *sciebas*.","verified")
n("n641","s038-02","amore","la","textual","*amore*, A: read *aurore* with B (*aurorae*, Job 38:12 Vulg.). A's misreading (*m* for *ur*) produces nonsense (‘with love’).","verified")
n("n642","s038-02","quem doctor subtilis","la","textual","*quem* A; *quam* B (agreeing with *auctoritas*). B's reading is grammatically preferable; this is a minor variant.","verified")
n("n643","s038-04","6. phisicorum","la","source","Motion as the act of the mobile passing from potency to act: Aristotle, *Phys.* III 1, 201a10–11 (definition of motion). Book VI deals with the divisibility of change. B also reads *vi.*","to-verify")
n("n644","s038-05","Ambrosium primo de trini. c. 6°.","la","source","Ambrose, *De fide* I (the Lombard's *Sent.* I d. 9 c. 4 cites it as *De Trinitate*): *si pater prius erat… generationis accessione mutatus est. Avertat Deus hanc amentiam*. The *in littera* is the Lombard's text, *Sent.* I d. 9.","to-verify")
n("n645","s038-05","auctoritas Hylarii in littera","la","source","Hilary, *De Trin.* XII (on ‘between begetting and being begotten there is no interval’), as cited in the Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 9.","to-verify")
n("n646","s038-05","distinctione quinta. q. 2.","la","source","Cross-reference to *Ord.* I d. 5 p. 2 q. un. (whether the Son is generated from the substance of the Father), on generation not being *mutatio*; cf. section 030 above.","to-verify")
n("n647","s038-07","Thomiste","la","historical","‘the Thomists’: Aquinas, *ST* I q. 42 a. 3 (*ordo naturae* without priority among the persons). Gorris names the school, not Thomas.","to-verify")
n("n648","s038-07","Aug. li. de fide ad Petrum","la","source","*De fide ad Petrum* is by Fulgentius of Ruspe, transmitted under Augustine's name, as the medievals commonly took it. The quoted sentence on the persons (*nullus eorum… praecedit… excedit… superat*) is to be located. B reads *eternitate et excedit* for A's *aut*.","to-verify")
n("n649","s038-08","omelia. 18.","la","source","The comment on John 16:13 (*audiet… audivit… audit*) is Augustine, *In Iohannis evangelium tractatus* 99.4–5, not tractate 18. Gorris's *omelia 18* is to be checked; possibly a corrupt numeral.","to-verify")
n("n650","s038-08","magister adducit di. 8. c. 2.","la","source","Peter Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 8 c. 1–2: of God properly only *est* is said, not *fuit* or *erit*. The Master's discussion of tenses applied to God.","to-verify")
n("n651","s038-08","pro tota questione","la","textual","A's abbreviation is ambiguous between *per* and *pro*; B's sign reads as *pro*.","to-verify")
n("n652","s038-01","day-star","en","translation","*lucifer*: the morning star (Ps. 109:3), rendered as in Douay.")
n("n653","s038-02","show the dawn its place","en","translation","Translating the correct reading *aurore* (B, Vulg.), not A's *amore*.")
n("n654","s038-06","being of existence","en","translation","*esse existentie* (common to the persons) vs *esse subsistentie* (proper to each).")

# --- B collation (full): B54L–B55L
upd("n640", text="A has *Sciebas* in the first quotation and *Sciebat* in the second. B has the same, *Sciebas* first and *Sciebat* second (B checked). The Vulgate (Job 38:21) reads *sciebas*.")
n("n971","s038-02","moralium. 29. sumpta","la","textual","B: *moral. xxix. supra quam doctor subtilis*. In B the relative clause is attached by *supra*, not by A's *sumpta*. Both give acceptable sense, and the translation follows A.","certain")
n("n972","s038-06","cum duratio respiciat esse existentie","la","textual","B adds *non dico subsistentie* here as well as after the second *esse existentie*.","certain")
n("n973","s038-08","siue significent actus personales","la","textual","B: *siue significent personales* (om. *actus*).","certain")
